guide forever/class/priest/blood-of-morphaz
title Blood of Morphaz
category Class
class Priest
folder Priest
levels 50-52
zone Azshara
keywords Cenarion Aid, Of Coursers We Know, The Ichor of Undeath, Blood of Morphaz, Ogtinc, Greta Mosshoof, Morphaz, Hazzas, Sunken Temple, Temple of Atal'Hakkar, Healthy Courser Gland, Ichor of Undeath, Blessed Prayer Beads, Circle of Hope, Woestave, class quest
reward text 17,060 experience and 1 gold 55 silver
why 17,060 XP and 1g55s at 50: Azshara, then Morphaz in the Sunken Temple (group of 5). The item choice may be gone.

# The level 52 Priest class chain: Cenarion Aid (8254) from a capital's
# priest trainer to Ogtinc in Azshara, then Of Coursers We Know (8255), The
# Ichor of Undeath (8256) and Blood of Morphaz (8257), handed in to Greta
# Mosshoof in Felwood.
# Givers of Cenarion Aid: Forever's quest data (quest 8254) lists Brother
# Joshua (Stormwind), High Priest Rohan (Ironforge) and Ur'kyo (Orgrimmar);
# the guide uses Rohan when you are in Ironforge, else Joshua (Alliance).
# Rewards: Forever's change notes for Blood of Morphaz (data/local/
# quest-audit/: "Rewards: no longer Choice of Blessed Prayer Beads, Choice of
# Circle of Hope, Choice of Woestave") say the item choice is gone, but the
# same quest page and another Forever database still list the three items
# (unnamed on the page; Forever's client has no names for them yet), so the
# guide promises only what is sure: 510 + 5100 + 5100 + 6350 = 17,060 XP and
# 1g55s (15500 copper on 8257, Forever's Priest class quest list), and says
# to look at the reward window. The reference data's reward spell on 8257
# (9884, a Mark of the Wild rank) is most likely a buff Greta casts on you,
# not a spell you learn: the card shows the experience and gold instead.
# INGAME: does Blood of Morphaz (8257) still offer Blessed Prayer Beads, Circle of Hope or Woestave on Forever, or experience and gold only?
# Drops (items.json, KB drops): Healthy Courser Gland 33% from Mosshoof
# Coursers (level 52-53, not elite, enrage at 30% health, respawn about 5.5
# minutes); Ichor of Undeath from undead everywhere, best Anguished and
# Suffering Highborne in Winterspring (level 54-55, about 13%), Lingering
# Highborne in Azshara's Ruins of Eldarath (level 48, about 10%), Highborne
# Apparitions and Lichlings on the Ashenvale border of Azshara (level 45-46,
# about 8-9%); Blood of Morphaz 100% from Morphaz.
# Morphaz: a level 52 elite green dragon with Hazzas (53) in the Sunken
# Temple's Pit of Sacrifice. The order (Classic dungeon guides, Warcraft
# Tavern's Temple of Atal'hakkar guide): six troll minibosses, Jammal'an,
# Weaver and Dreamscythe, then Morphaz and Hazzas appear together and cannot
# be pulled apart. The data has no position for
# Morphaz or the entrance; the entrance point (69,54, the temple ruins in
# the middle of the Pool of Tears) is from players' reports, the path in
# (south steps, under the water, down the stairs) from several walkthroughs.
# Players' reports on 8257: loot him in a party, not a raid group, or the
# blood may not drop.
# Ogtinc's cliff: quest notes (leave the road at the fork before the ruins
# and follow the north cliff edge; the naga ruins and the beach below have
# no way up).
# Based on data, not play: the beta caps at level 30 until launch on
# 4 November, so nothing here has been checked in game.

step Cenarion Aid: High Priest Rohan
  only Alliance
  when zone "Ironforge"
  when !onquest 8254
  zone Ironforge
  tip At 50 in Ironforge, High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries (Mystic Ward) offers Cenarion Aid. Before you leave a city, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
  level 50
  accept 8254 npc 11406                       -- High Priest Rohan

step Cenarion Aid: Brother Joshua
  only Alliance
  when !onquest 8254
  zone Stormwind City
  tip At 50, Brother Joshua at the altar of Stormwind's Cathedral of Light offers Cenarion Aid (High Priest Rohan in Ironforge has it too). Before you leave, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House in the Trade District (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
  level 50
  accept 8254 npc 5489                        -- Brother Joshua

step Cenarion Aid: Ur'kyo
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip At 50, Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits offers Cenarion Aid. Before you leave, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
  level 50
  accept 8254 npc 6018                        -- Ur'kyo

step Ogtinc
  zone Azshara
  tip Ogtinc, a furbolg, lives on the clifftop north-east of the Ruins of Eldarath. Alliance: fly to Talrendis Point; Horde: fly to Valormok. Ride east and leave the road at the fork before the ruins, then follow the northern cliff edge east to him: the naga ruins and the beach below are walled in by cliffs with no way up.
  getfp "Talrendis Point" only Alliance
  getfp "Valormok" only Horde
  turnin 8254                                 -- Ogtinc
  accept 8255

step Of Coursers We Know
  tip Mosshoof Coursers (level 52-53, not elite) graze all over Azshara, thickest north-east of Ogtinc and south of the mountains; about one in three drops a Healthy Courser Gland, so plan on a dozen kills for four. They enrage at 30% health: finish them fast. Killing them costs no Cenarion Circle reputation. Keep any Ichor of Undeath you loot.
  collect 20027 x4 quest 8255.1               -- Healthy Courser Gland

step Ogtinc
  turnin 8255                                 -- Ogtinc
  accept 8256

step The Ichor of Undeath
  tip Carrying an Ichor of Undeath already? It counts at once. Otherwise any undead may drop one, rarely: the Lingering Highborne (level 48) in the Ruins of Eldarath below Ogtinc's cliff drop it about one kill in ten, the highborne ghosts on Azshara's border with Ashenvale (level 45-46) a little less, the Anguished and Suffering Highborne in Winterspring (54-55) about one in eight. The Auction House is usually quicker.
  collect 7972 quest 8256.1                   -- Ichor of Undeath

step Ogtinc
  turnin 8256                                 -- Ogtinc
  accept 8257

step Morphaz in the Sunken Temple
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip Morphaz is a level 52 elite green dragon inside the Sunken Temple, a five-player dungeon: bring a group of five (a level 60 group clears it with ease). Horde: fly to Stonard; Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands and ride north. The temple stands in the middle of the Pool of Tears: climb the steps on its south side, swim down through the flooded hall and take the stairs to the portal. Inside, Morphaz only appears late: kill the six troll minibosses on the upper balconies, then Jammal'an the Prophet below them; that wakes the drakes Weaver and Dreamscythe in the Pit of Sacrifice, and killing both brings Morphaz and Hazzas. The pair patrols together and cannot be split: pull them into a hallway and have the tank face them away from the group (breath and a knockback). Loot him in a party, not a raid group: the blood always drops.
  collect 20025 quest 8257.1 @69.0,54.0 group 5 -- Blood of Morphaz: the Sunken Temple entrance

step Greta Mosshoof
  zone Felwood
  tip Greta Mosshoof is at the Emerald Sanctuary in southern Felwood. Horde: fly to Bloodvenom Post and ride south-east; Alliance: fly to Astranaar in Ashenvale and ride north into Felwood. She takes the blood for experience and gold. Look at the reward window before you hand in: Classic let you pick Blessed Prayer Beads, Circle of Hope or Woestave, and Forever's notes say that choice may be gone.
  turnin 8257                                 -- Greta Mosshoof
